IMPLEMENTED 2026-08-14 on branch fix/9kwzp-auth-posture, commit 351f40bd. NOT closed: the epic PR is opened by the orchestrator and work is not complete until it merges.

backend/tests/test_auth_exempt_paths_snapshot.py, 23 tests:
  * exact-set snapshot, grouped as main.py groups them, whose failure message IS the reviewer checklist (5 questions for an added path, 1 for a removed one) rather than a set diff alone;
  * per-path restatement so a removal reads as a route name in CI output;
  * two shape assertions -- every entry is under /api/, and none carries a trailing slash, query string or uppercase. Both catch entries that can NEVER match the middleware's exact-string test and so grant nothing while reading as a reviewed grant;
  * test_exempt_paths_that_carry_their_own_dependency -- GET and PUT /api/auth/admin/settings are middleware-exempt but chain get_current_user via auth.routes.require_admin, so they enforce in every mode. Pinned by walking the live dependency tree, because reading the exempt set alone overstates the exposure, and because that protection is one Depends away from being deleted by somebody who reads the exemption and concludes the route is meant to be public. If it fails, the route that toggles require_auth just became anonymous.

tests/integration/test_api_auth.py:568-581 was NOT misleading in what it asserts, but was incomplete in what it disclaimed. Annotated rather than changed: it now states that it proves nothing about the auth-enabled case (which the new snapshot covers) and that 200-in-setup-mode is no longer a general rule (bead jy006 gates three primitives even then, and /api/settings is deliberately not one of them).

