The PO's minimum supported viewport is 1280x720. Every @media in the modal CSS estate targets a width at or below 820px, so none can ever fire for a supported user:

  @media (max-width: 600px)  x6
  @media (max-width: 820px)  x1
  @media (max-width: 700px)  x1
  @media (max-width: 500px)  x1

Nine blocks of unreachable CSS carrying real declarations, which read as live responsive behaviour to anyone maintaining these files. One was already a trap: ModalBase's max-width 600px header/body/footer padding block was dead for a SECOND reason (a media query adds no specificity, and StreamsPane declared the same selectors bare and unconditionally), and would have come alive as a side effect when bead 87o0c made ModalBase the chassis owner — silently shrinking every dialog's frame. It was deleted rather than resurrected.

Cleanup: delete the nine blocks, or if any encodes intent worth keeping, re-express it against a breakpoint inside the supported range. Worth checking the wider app for the same shape — this bead covers modal CSS only.

Not urgent. Dead code that cannot execute is a maintenance and comprehension cost, not a defect.
